WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.975
Why both?

2
00:00:00.975 --> 00:00:05.382
Learn's overview, What is Azure DDoS
Protection, says it works at layers

3
00:00:05.382 --> 00:00:09.713
three and four, and that layer seven
needs a web application firewall.

4
00:00:09.713 --> 00:00:12.688
So an internet-facing workload needs both.

5
00:00:12.688 --> 00:00:17.250
And each has to be in the mode that
acts, not only the mode that logs.

6
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:22.303
Learn's Zero Trust recommendations for
the Application Gateway web application

7
00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:26.167
firewall put it plainly: in
detection mode it logs and forwards;

8
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:27.950
only prevention mode blocks.

9
00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:32.737
A firewall left in detection mode is the
first danger in the guide's dangers table.

10
00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:38.039
So this module takes every public I P in
the register to DDoS protection with logs

11
00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:42.471
and an alert, and every web endpoint
to a firewall in prevention mode,

12
00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:45.700
tuned first so it doesn't
block legitimate users.
